          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Generally, a
            %em Berry phase
            is a non-trivial phase picked up by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+state"} quantum state
            of definite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/energy"} energy
            under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+adiabatic+theorem"} adiabatic
            changes of the
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+system"} quantum system
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian"} Hamiltonian
            around a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop"} loop
            in its parameter space.
          %p
            Specifically, in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+matter+theory"} condensed matter theory
            and for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystal"} crystalline
            material with a set of isolated (gapped)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electronic+band+structure"} electronic bands
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+derivatives"} partial derivatives
            along
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/momentum"} momentum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vectors"} vectors
            of the corresponding
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bloch+states"} Bloch states
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+vector+bundle"} connection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+1-form"} 1-form
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            (over the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brillouin+torus"} Brillouin torus
            = succeed "," do
              %em Berry connection
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Berry84"} Berry 84
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Simon83"} Simon 83
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+transport"} parallel transport
            along this connection describes the change of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bloch+states"} Bloch states
            under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+adiabatic+theorem"} adiabatic
            change of their
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/momentum"} momentum
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+vector"} wave vector
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature+2-form"} curvature 2-form
            of a Berry connection is accordingly called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em Berry curvature
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy"} holonomy
            of such a Berry connection is called a
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Berry+phase"} Berry phase
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zak+phase"} Zak phase
            (
            %a{:href => "#Zak89"}> Zak 89
            ) when evaluated along one of the non-trivial 1-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cycles"} cycles
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brillouin+torus"} Brillouin torus
          %p
            By default, this is understood to apply to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valence+bundle"} valence bundle
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystal"} crystalline
            material, but the construction works more generally.
          %p#TopologicalOrder
            If in the case of a gapped
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valence+bundle"} valence bundle
            = succeed "-phase," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+insulator"} topological insulator
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy"} holonomy
            of the Berry connection is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+group"} non-abelian
            (which may happen, as originally highlighted in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#WilczekZee1984"} Wilczek &amp; Zee 84
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+order"} topological order
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semimetals"} semimetals
            the Berry phases of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valence+bundle"} valence bundle
            around their nodal loci of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            2 are a measure for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruction
            to adiabatically deforming the semimetal such as to open its gap closures, hence to become a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+insulator"}> topological
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/insulator"} insulator
            (eg.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Vanderbilt18"} Vanderbilt 18, 5.5.2
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#hall_systems Hall systems
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hall+systems"} Hall systems
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                induces
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anomalous+velocity"} anomalous velocity
                of electrons and with it the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anomalous+Hall+effect"} anomalous Hall effect
              %p
                (here this is Berry curvature on the “reciprocal space”
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brillouin+torus"} Brillouin torus
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bloch+theory"} Bloch
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/momenta"} momenta
                in a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystal"} crystalline
                material),
            %li
              %p
                induces the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anyon"} anyon
                %a{:href => "quantum+Hall+effect#BraidingPhase"} braiding phase
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+quantum+Hall+systems"} fractional quantum Hall systems
                (see
                %a{:href => "Laughlin+wavefunction#BasicLaughlinStateWithQuasiHoles"} here
                at
                = succeed ")." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laughlin+wavefunction"} Laughlin wavefunction
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Berry%27s+phase"} Berry's phase
                (needs to be merged)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+adiabatic+theorem"} quantum adiabatic theorem
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The original article:
          %ul
            %li#Berry84
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+V.+Berry"}> Michael V. Berry
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantal phase factors accompanying adiabatic changes
              %strong 392
              (1984) 45–57 (
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1098/rspa.1984.0023"}> doi:10.1098/rspa.1984.0023
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2397741"} jstor:2397741
          %p
            The formulation in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connections"} connections
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundles"} fiber bundles
            and their
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy"} holonomy
          %ul
            %li#Simon83
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barry+Simon"}> Barry Simon
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Holonomy, the Quantum Adiabatic Theorem, and Berry’s Phase
              %strong 51
              (1983) 2167 (
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.51.2167"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.51.2167
              )
          %p
            Generalization to (connections with)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+group"} non-abelian
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomies"} holonomies
          %ul
            %li#WilczekZee1984
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Wilczek"}> Frank Wilczek
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anthony+Zee"} Anthony Zee
              = succeed "," do
                %em Appearance of gauge structure in simple dynamical systems
              %strong 52
              24 (1984) 2111
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.52.2111"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.52.2111
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %p
            The special case of Berry phases around the 1-cycles of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brillouin+torus"} Brillouin torus
            –
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zak+phases"} Zak phases
          %ul
            %li#Zak89
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joshua+Zak"}> Joshua Zak
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Berry’s phase for energy bands in solids
              %strong 62
              (1989) 2747 (
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.62.2747"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.62.2747
              )
          %p Review and further discussion:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Berry"}> Michael Berry
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The quantum phase, five years after
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometric phases in physics
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 5
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Berry-FiveYearsAfter.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/0613"} doi:10.1142/0613
            %li
              %p
                Ming-Che Chang, Qian Niu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Berry curvature, orbital moment, and effective quantum theory of electrons in electromagnetic fields
                %strong 20
                (2008) 193202 (
                %a{:href => "https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1088/0953-8984/20/19/193202"}> doi:10.1088/0953-8984/20/19/193202
                )
            %li#XiaoChangNiu10
              %p
                Di Xiao, Ming-Che Chang, Qian Niu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Berry Phase Effects on Electronic Properties
                %strong 82
                (2010) 1959-2007 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0907.2021"}> arXiv:0907.2021
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/RevModPhys.82.1959"} doi:10.1103/RevModPhys.82.1959
          %p
            With focus on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+phases+of+matter"} topological phases of matter
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+insulators"}> topological insulators
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semimetals"} semimetals
          %ul
            %li#Vanderbilt18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Vanderbilt"}> David Vanderbilt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Berry Phases in Electronic Structure Theory – Electric Polarization, Orbital Magnetization and Topological Insulators
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/9781316662205"} doi:10.1017/9781316662205
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%A9r%C3%B4me+Cayssol"}> Jérôme Cayssol
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-No%C3%ABl+Fuchs"} Jean-Noël Fuchs
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topological and geometrical aspects of band theory
                %strong 4
                (2021) 034007 (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.11941"}> arXiv:2012.11941
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/2515-7639/abf0b5"} doi:10.1088/2515-7639/abf0b5
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tudor+D.+Stanescu"}> Tudor D. Stanescu
                , Chapter 2 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to Topological Quantum Matter &amp; Quantum Computation
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.routledge.com/Introduction-to-Topological-Quantum-Matter--Quantum-Computation/Stanescu/p/book/9780367574116"} ISBN:9780367574116
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berry_connection_and_curvature"} Berry connection and curvature
          %p
            Berry curvature in momentum space is closely analogous to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+field"} magnetic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+density"} flux density
            – the ordinary
            = succeed "-term" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+force"} Lorentz force
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anomalous+velocity"} anomalous velocity
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#XiaoChangNiu10"} Xiao, Chang and Niu 2010 §III.A
            %li
              %p
                Y. D. Chong:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Berry’s phase and the anomalous velocity of Bloch wavepackets
                %strong 81
                (2010) 052303 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0912.0716"}> arXiv:0912.0716
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.81.052303"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevB.81.052303
            %li
              %p
                Michael Stone:
                %em Berry Curvature, Spin, and Anomalous Velocity
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.thp.uni-koeln.de/ESI-Web/slides/Stone.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Stone-BerryCurvature.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %h3#for_anyon_statistics For anyon statistics
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anyon+statistics"} anyon phases
            (specifically in the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+Hall+effect"} quantum Hall effect
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Berry+phases"} Berry phases
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+adiabatic+theorem"} adiabatic
            transport of anyon positions:
          %ul
            %li#AvrosSchriefferWilczek84
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+P.+Arovas"}> Daniel P. Arovas
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Robert+Schrieffer"} John Robert Schrieffer
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Wilczek"} Frank Wilczek
              = succeed "," do
                %em Fractional Statistics and the Quantum Hall Effect
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.53.722"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.53.722
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %h3#experimental_observation Experimental observation
          %p
            Experimental observation of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zak+phases"} Zak phases
          %ul
            %li
              Marcos Atala, Monika Aidelsburger, Julio T. Barreiro, Dmitry Abanin, Takuya Kitagawa, Eugene Demler, Immanuel Bloch:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Direct measurement of the Zak phase in topological Bloch bands
              %strong 9
              (2013) 795–800 (
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1038/nphys2790"}> doi:10.1038/nphys2790
              )
          %p
            Proposal for experimental realization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Berry+phases"} Berry phases
            around
            = succeed "=2" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-metals"} semi-metals
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Dan-Wei Zhang, Y. X. Zhao, Rui-Bin Liu, Zheng-Yuan Xue, Shi-Liang Zhu, Z. D. Wang,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum simulation of exotic PT-invariant topological nodal loop bands with ultracold atoms in an optical lattice
                %strong 93
                (2016) 043617 (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1601.00371"}> arXiv:1601.00371
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevA.93.043617"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevA.93.043617
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (see sec II.A, these authors stand out as mentioning the relevant
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO-theory"} KO-theory
        .revisedby
